### 1.3 Context Virtualization (Virtual Memory Paging)

Standard LLM architectures suffer from an inherent tension: large context windows (128k to 1M+ tokens) suffer from catastrophic attention degradation (the *Lost in the Middle* phenomenon), quadratic compute scaling, and memory bloat. Conversely, aggressive truncation leads to amnesia, losing critical system directives and security invariants established at task initialization.

To overcome this without reliance on infinite physical context, APEX introduces **Context Virtualization (OS-Style Context Paging)**:

```
